# Everything JARVIS writes at runtime is machine-local. Ignore the lot, then
# re-admit the two files that are genuinely part of the repo.
#
# The reason this is a blanket rule and not a list: `jarvis/tool-token` is the
# bearer token guarding POST /internal/tool — the only thing standing between a
# local process and every acting tool JARVIS has. It lives here because
# JARVIS_DATA_DIR defaults inside the repo, and this repository is public. A
# single `git add -A` would have published it. Deny by default; allow by name.
*
!.gitkeep
!.gitignore
